00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.830 align:start position:0%
environment ministers will discuss  sustainability issues linked to the  development of the energy Union when  they meet in Russells on march six the  energy union is a major project aiming  to reform how europe produces transports  and consumes energy ministers will  examine how best to achieve that change  for instance by using more energy from  renewable sources and becoming more  energy efficient the outcome of the  debate will be forwarded to the  President of the European Council ahead  of the March meeting of EU leaders  ministers will also continue  preparations for the UN climate change  conference taking place in Paris in  December this conference aims to adopt a  new legally binding agreement on climate  change they will also have an exchange  of views on the post-2015 agenda it  should establish the new global  partnership for poverty eradication and  sustainable development due to be  adopted by the UN in September a deal in  this agenda will also have important  implications for negotiations on the new  climate change agreement
 

